§ `Tests -- s 30C(1): days and periods of incapacity for work`

#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(a) the day is a day of incapacity for work` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(a) the day is a day of incapacity for work` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(a) the day is a day of incapacity for work` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): 4 or more consecutive days, each a day of incapacity (1 to 4 January is 4 days; 1 to 3 January is 3)
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(b) the run of days is a period of incapacity for work` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 4 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(b) the run of days is a period of incapacity for work` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 3 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(b) the run of days is a period of incapacity for work` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 4 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(b) the run of days is a period of incapacity for work` (Date 29 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c): two periods separated by 8 weeks (56 days) or less are one; period A is 1 to 10 January 2025
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(c) the two periods are treated as one period of incapacity for work` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 11 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(c) the two periods are treated as one period of incapacity for work` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 8 3 2025) (Date 20 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(c) the two periods are treated as one period of incapacity for work` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 9 3 2025) (Date 20 3 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- overlapping periods are not separated at all
#ASSERT `s 30C(1)(c) the two periods are treated as one period of incapacity for work` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 5 1 2025) (Date 20 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 30C(1)(c) the period of incapacity for work that the two periods are treated as` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 8 3 2025) (Date 20 3 2025))) EQUALS JUST (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 20 3 2025))
#ASSERT (`s 30C(1)(c) the period of incapacity for work that the two periods are treated as` (`s 30C test period from` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025)) (`s 30C test period from` (Date 9 3 2025) (Date 20 3 2025))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30C(7) the number of days in a week` EQUALS 7

